UBI provides a financial safety net, allowing individuals to take risks such as starting a business or pursuing education without the fear of losing their income.
By removing the need to take on unstable or exploitative jobs, UBI can lead to more meaningful and productive work, enhancing overall economic participation.
Studies from pilot programs show that UBI can increase employment rates and entrepreneurial activity by reducing financial stress and increasing confidence in the workforce.
UBI can reduce poverty and inequality, which in turn fosters a more stable and dynamic economy where more people can contribute meaningfully.
When people are not worried about basic needs, they are more likely to engage in creative, innovative, and community-driven activities that benefit the economy.